# Cline → repository guidance (routing only)

This file only *points at* guidance that already lives in this repo. Nothing is
copied here, so edit the source files, never this index. Read `AGENT.md` first;
it is authoritative.

Read in this order:

1. `README.md` — what the project is, CLI usage, web player.
2. `AGENT.md` — intent, invariants that must not break, interfaces, committing
   and publishing, adding a rule, adding a puzzle family, measured rule
   coverage, known gaps.
3. `docs/model-and-puzzle-formats.md` — exact family syntax and file formats.
4. `docs/puzzle-collection.md` — collection and grading notes.
5. `RELEASE_NOTES.md` — changelog, breaking changes, migration notes.

Task-specific skills (GitHub Copilot skill files — read the matching one before
authoring or transcribing any puzzle):

- `.github/skills/non-murdoku-puzzle-authoring/SKILL.md` — every family except
  Murdoku; use `puzzle-lab` (`fresh`, `generate`, `rate`, `search`, `audit`).
- `.github/skills/murdoku-puzzle-generator/SKILL.md` — Murdoku only; its own
  tools and workflow.

Repo tooling rather than reasoning: validate with `uv run csp <files>`,
`--brute-force`, `--grade`, and `uv run puzzle-lab`. Tests: `uv run pytest`.
